    outlook: "Following their Oscar dominance, 'One Battle After Another' and 'Sinners' are poised for extended runs in theaters and highly anticipated releases on major streaming platforms, likely driving significant subscriber growth. Director Elias Vance and the leading actors are expected to be inundated with new projects, potentially shaping the next decade of cinema. The industry will closely watch how studios respond to this trend, perhaps greenlighting more character-driven dramas and fewer big-budget spectacles in the immediate future. Expect intense speculation for the 2027 awards season to begin almost immediately, with critics already debating which emerging talents might follow in this year's winners' footsteps. Film festivals across the globe will be on the lookout for similar powerful narratives.",
    conclusion: "The 98th Academy Awards will be remembered as the year 'One Battle After Another' and 'Sinners' cemented their places in cinematic history. Their sweeping victories are a testament to compelling storytelling, masterful direction, and unforgettable performances, resonating with a global audience. As the dust settles in Hollywood, the impact of these films will undoubtedly ripple across the industry, inspiring future generations of filmmakers and shaping the cultural discourse around cinema for years to come. The Oscar statuettes now stand as beacons, celebrating the enduring power of film to entertain, provoke, and unite.",
